        "notes": "Async generator declarations, expressions, object methods, and class methods materialize as generated non-constructable JsFunctionObject instances. Every call creates an independent AsyncGeneratorScope and AsyncGeneratorObject while retaining shared lexical captures and the call-time receiver. Parameter binding runs synchronously when called. Known limitations: throw() and return() protocol methods have known issues; try/catch/finally with async generators may generate invalid IL in some cases. The native Test262 harness now verifies 143 additional async-generator expression cases, including parameter binding, destructuring, and static early errors."
      },
